344	  // routinely a file the agent did not author: `templates/conversations/*.json`
345	  // is exactly what CLAUDE.md points agents at ("Modèles prêts à copier"), and
346	  // a template saved from the dashboard carries an `origin` of its own. Skipping
347	  // the resolver there stamped an agent-created conversation with whatever that
348	  // file happened to hold — at a rank the hook (3) and the backfill (1) can
349	  // never take back. The MCP twin already decided this the other way and says
350	  // so in its own comment (`server/mcp/hubWriteTools.ts`, `convo_create`):
351	  // re-resolve every time, and feed the caller's origin in as `explicit` input
352	  // (shape-validated, never trusted verbatim) rather than as the answer.
353	  //
354	  // Priority for the resolver's `explicit` input: the `--origin-json` flag
355	  // (this command's own argument, the most deliberate signal) > a
356	  // payload-supplied `origin` > plain env detection.
357	  //
